# `bundles/` above has no leading slash, so it matches a directory of that name at any
# depth, and the documentation has a section about bundles. Those four pages are source
# and git was silently declining to track them. The broad pattern stays, because a run
# written into a subdirectory is still output nobody should commit.
!docs/bundles/

